{
  "meta": {
    "note": "The three intro animations, as geometry rather than as pictures. One ball crosses each frame and leaves a yellow trail that draws the idea: a pass from one club to the next, a run that settles on the right answer, a climb that bursts into stars. Both apps render this with their own vector primitives, so it costs no image bytes and stays sharp at any density.",
    "why-shared": "The numbers live here for the same reason the design tokens do. Two hand-tuned copies of an arc are two different arcs within a month, and nobody would notice until the two stores were showing two different intros.",
    "frame": "408x200 is the slot: 200 tall, and as wide as the column allows, which is 408 at most and 370 on a 402dp phone. The renderers scale to fill and centre, so the sides are what gets cropped. Everything that matters stays inside a 24 margin."
  },
